{"t": 1792732653590, "cmd": "note", "args": ["--shot", "winter_end", "Winter (tick 171002-231003) ended with 16 NPC hunger deaths across 7 nations (Upperville 5, Fortwood 4, Fortresston 2, Yellowshire 2, Forttown/Blueburg/Southernville 1 each), every one 'within the walls' of a settlement. Deaths only appear as chronicle lines mixed in with raids and stalls; there is no per-settlement food meter, famine warning, or alert before the first death, and pawns' hunger/energy is not visible on screen. Meanwhile trees kept giving apples in winter so the player never went hungry (apples 30->41)."]}
